   "evidence": "`Iterated.lean` puts no `\u03b1 \u2264 1` hypothesis on `CkHolderSpace`. Only lemmas like `holderWith_iteratedFDeriv_of_le (h\u03b1 : \u03b1 \u2264 1)` assume it, at Iterated.lean:379.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Holder/LowOrder.lean",
   "fix": "Qualify the sentence, e.g. 'In general they are not equal: for `\u03b1 \u2264 1`, at order one the sum norm exceeds the maximum norm by ..., which is `\u2016sin\u2016_\u221e = 1` for `f = sin` on `\u211d`.'",
   "issue": "The module docstring says the norms 'are not equal' and cites `f = sin` on `\u211d`, with no condition on `\u03b1`. `CkHolderSpace` allows any `\u03b1 : \u211d\u22650`. For `\u03b1 > 1`, `cos` is not globally `\u03b1`-H\u00f6lder, so `sin` is not in the space. In that case every element of `CkHolderSpace 1 \u03b1 \u211d F` is constant, because `Df` is constant and `f` is bounded, and the sum norm then equals the max norm. The claim overreaches.",
   "line": 26
  }
 ],
